
# ======================
# Repo metadata
# ======================
.git
.gitignore
README.md

# The rest of the repo-root prose. README.md was already listed; these were
# not, so `stow .` symlinked all seven into $HOME -- ~/TROUBLESHOOTING.md,
# ~/plan_ui_ux_qtile.md, ~/qtile-veil-HANDOFF.md and the rest, as top-level
# files in a fresh user's home directory. Nothing reads them from there:
# rofi_docs opens them out of $DOTFILES.
#
# Patterned, not named one by one: the list was already out of date the first
# time it was written, and the next plan_*.md added to the repo root would
# have gone straight back into $HOME.
plan_.*\.md
qtile-.*\.md
THEME_AUDIT_REPORT.md
TROUBLESHOOTING.md

# Claude Code's PER-PROJECT state directory. It is not a dotfile, and it is a
# directory stow will fold into the user's existing ~/.claude rather than skip
# -- which is exactly what happened here: ~/.claude/worktrees is a symlink
# back into this repo, inside the user's global Claude config.
.claude

# ======================
# Images / assets
# ======================
IMGS

# The GitHub Pages manual. A directory, so stow would link ~/docs into a
# fresh user's home the same way it once linked the repo-root prose. It is
# read on the web (and out of the repo), never out of $HOME.
docs

